From: shuuri-labs <61762328+shuuri-labs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: pm8150: add the bootloader and recovery
 reboot modes

Without reboot modes on the PON, `reboot bootloader` is a plain restart, so
Linux cannot open the bootloader's menu. The Qualcomm ABL reads 0x2 as
bootloader and 0x1 as recovery; sm8250 boards that need them set the same
values one board at a time (sony-xperia-edo, xiaomi-elish), and pmk8550.dtsi
carries them for every sm8550 board.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8150.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8150.dtsi
@@ -49,6 +49,8 @@
 		pon: pon@800 {
 			compatible = "qcom,pm8998-pon";
 			reg = <0x0800>;
+			mode-bootloader = <0x2>;
+			mode-recovery = <0x1>;
 
 			pon_pwrkey: pwrkey {
 				compatible = "qcom,pm8941-pwrkey";
